{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nProf. Vasechkin wants to represent positive integer n as a sum of addends, where each addends is an integer number containing only 1s. For example, he can represent 121 as 121=111+11+\u20131. Help him to find the least number of digits 1 in such sum.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++ code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include<vector>\n#include<string>\n#include<algorithm>\n#include<iostream>\n#include <iomanip>\n#include<cmath>\n#include<cstdlib>\n#include<cstdio>\n#include<stack>\n#include<queue>\n#include<cstring>\n#include<map>\n#include<set>\nusing namespace std;\n#define MOD 1000000007\nint a[1111111];\nlong long x[30];\nlong long now=6;\nint cal(long long n)\n{\n\tint l=0;\n\tif(n<0)\n\t\tn=-n;\n\tif(n<=now)\n\t\treturn a[n];\n\tlong long last;\n\tlong long t=n;\n\twhile(t>0)\n\t{\n\t\tl++;\n\t\tlast=t;\n\t\tt/=10;\n\t}\n\tif(last<=5)\n\t{\n\t\tif(n>=x[l]*last||last==1)\n\t\t\treturn cal(n-x[l]*last)+last*l;\n\t\telse\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tint r1,r2;\n\t\t\tr1=cal(x[l]*last-n)+last*l;\n\t\t\tr2=cal(n-x[l]*(last-1))+(last-1)*l;\n\t\t\treturn min(r1,r2);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\telse if(last>6)\n\t\treturn cal(x[l+1]-n)+l+1;\n\telse\n\t{\n\t\tint r1,r2;\n\t\tif(n>x[l]*last)\n\t\t\tr1=cal(n-x[l]*last)+last*l;\n\t\telse\n\t\t\tr1=cal(x[l]*last-n)+last*l;\n\t\tr2=cal(n-x[l]*(last-1))+(last-1)*l;\n\t\tr1=min(r1,r2);\n\t\tr2=cal(x[l+1]-n)+l+1;\n\t\treturn min(r1,r2);\n\t}\n}\nint main()\n{\n\tint i;\n\tlong long n;\n\tcin>>n;\n\tx[1]=1;\n\tfor(i=2;i<=15;i++)\n\t{\n\t\tx[i]=x[i-1]*10+1;\n\t}\n\tfor(i=0;i<7;i++)\n\t\ta[i]=i;\n\tfor(i=7;i<1111110;i++)\n\t{\n\t\ta[i]=cal(i);\n\t\tnow=i;\n\t}\n\tif(n<1111110)\n\t\tcout<<a[n]<<endl;\n\telse\n\t{\n\t\tcout<<cal(n)<<endl;\n\t}\n\t//system(\"pause\");\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include<vector>\n#include<string>\n#include<algorithm>\n#include<iostream>\n#include <iomanip>\n#include<cmath>\n#include<cstdlib>\n#include<cstdio>\n#include<stack>\n#include<queue>\n#include<cstring>\n#include<map>\n#include<set>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long x[20];\n\nlong long cal(long long n) {\n    if (n == 0) return 0;\n    if (n < 0) return cal(-n);\n    \n    string s = to_string(n);\n    int len = s.length();\n    \n    if (len == 1) {\n        return n;\n    }\n    \n    long long first_digit = s[0] - '0';\n    long long all_ones = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n        all_ones = all_ones * 10 + 1;\n    }\n    \n    long long option1 = first_digit * len + cal(n - first_digit * all_ones);\n    \n    long long option2 = (10 - first_digit) * len + cal((first_digit + 1) * all_ones - n);\n    \n    return min(option1, option2);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    \n    cout << cal(n) << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.768370445162873e-07, -0.0002227773511549458, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.0609570381348021e-05, -0.143756151199